l/agent/factory.md", "line": 172, "text": "Any other scheme raises `ValueError` (`unsupported database scheme: \u2026 (expected sqlite/mysql)`). Config loading already refuses every scheme other than `mysql`,"}, {"file": "docs/internal/agent/factory.md", "line": 174, "text": "`statement_timeout_ms`, `max_rows`, and `read_only` are threaded as keyword arguments into every runner. `read_only` (default `True`) causes each connector to e"}, {"file": "docs/internal/agent/factory.md", "line": 176, "text": "`sqlglot_dialect_for_url(url)` (in `sqllens.safety`) maps the same scheme to a sqlglot dialect name (`\"sqlite\"`, `\"mysql\"`) that `build_agent` hands to the read"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/cleanup-error-handling.md", "line": 22, "text": "The runner wraps the write-path `cursor.close()` and the final `conn.close()` in `try / except Exception` and logs and swallows the secondary error so the **pri"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/cleanup-error-handling.md", "line": 32, "text": "The read path streams through an `SSDictCursor` and deliberately never calls `cursor.close()` on it: closing a server-side cursor drains every remaining row fro"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/cleanup-error-handling.md", "line": 36, "text": "1. **`except Exception`, not `except BaseException`.** `KeyboardInterrupt`, `SystemExit`, and `asyncio.CancelledError` inherit from `BaseException`, not `Except"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/cleanup-error-handling.md", "line": 46, "text": "Regression coverage lives in [`tests/unit/test_sql_runner_cleanup.py`](../../../tests/unit/test_sql_runner_cleanup.py):"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 11, "text": "1. **Parser guard** \u2014 `assert_select_only` / `ReadOnlyGuardRunner` rejects anything that isn't a single `SELECT` / `WITH` (plus an allowlist of structural read-"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 12, "text": "2. **Driver-level read-only** \u2014 when `database.read_only = true` (the default), each connector enforces read-only at the session/connection layer before any use"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 33, "text": "- **`TABLE t` is refused.** MySQL's `TABLE t` shorthand for `SELECT * FROM t` is rejected on every supported sqlglot version: sqlglot parses it as an alias befo"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 37, "text": "6. **Reject `SELECT ... INTO`.** MySQL's `SELECT ... INTO @var` writes a session variable; on T-SQL, `SELECT * INTO new_tbl FROM users` creates `new_tbl`. sqlgl"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/read-only-safety.md", "line": 38, "text": "7. **Reject side-effecting / DoS / RCE functions.** A syntactically valid `SELECT` can still call `load_extension` (SQLite RCE), `load_file` (MySQL data exfiltr"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/row-level-security.md", "line": 30, "text": "- A `TABLE orders` query, in any statement or subquery (MySQL shorthand for `SELECT * FROM orders`). sqlglot parses it differently before and from 30.30, so `ap"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/row-level-security.md", "line": 46, "text": "**Database-defined routines (MySQL).** `_called_names` reads the rewritten SQL with sqlglot's tokenizer under the connection's dialect and collects every name w"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/row-level-security.md", "line": 106, "text": "The whole statement is printed again by sqlglot (`tree.sql(dialect=..., normalize_functions=False)` in `apply_rls`), not patched in place. Function names sqlglo"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/row-level-security.md", "line": 225, "text": "- Connection-level relation checks raise a sanitized `RlsError` when a view, unverified relation or call whose name matches a database-defined routine is encoun"}, {"file": "docs/internal/mcp-server/transport.md", "line": 117, "text": "- **SQL execution.** The SQLite and MySQL runners' `run_sql` coroutines hand their synchronous driver work (`connect`, the row-level-security relation check tha"}], "audit_hints_truncated": true, "views": {"head": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-387/local-20261113T080923Z-1-shadow/view-head", "revision": "8d683649aa78fe8f1b748fb378782ce231fc4f00"}, "base": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-387/local-20261113T080923Z-1-shadow/view-base", "revision": "c4cbde0e5005950492dcad45f8ef5fa84a8b8fa1"}}, "dependency_sources": [], "pr": {"number": "387", "body": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-387/local-20261113T080923Z-1-shadow/pr-body.md", "head_ref": "worktree-issue-382", "base_ref": "main", "api_head_sha": "8d683649aa78fe8f1b748fb378782ce231fc4f00", "author_trust": "trusted"}, "issue": {"number": "382", "source": "override", "context": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-387/local-20261113T080923Z-1-shadow/issue-context.md"}, "warnings": []}
